<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Rail offers dip, soft exports.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Rail offers dip, soft exports.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>A modest slowdown in the U.S. soybean meal export market was pressuring railcar basis offers on Tuesday, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The exports are starting to soften just a little bit,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>The soymeal truck market remained underpinned by solid domestic demand, especially from poultry producers on the East Coast, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's turkey season and domestic use should remain firm because of the holiday and the cold weather,&quot; one southeastern broker said.</p>
<p>Supplies of soymeal were also said to be easing somewhat in various markets, which also contributed to the falling basis levels, cash sources said.</p>
<p>&quot;The processors all seem to have product for sale now,&quot; one broker said.  </p>
